+/// Pointers handed to a host-function callback are valid only for that synchronous C++ call.
+/// The callback enters `JavaScriptActor` synchronously, so this wrapper never escapes or crosses
+/// a thread. Swift 6.2 nevertheless requires an explicit unchecked sendability boundary here.
+private final class HostFunctionCallPointers: @unchecked Sendable {
